rule c1xx: a default argument is built at EVERY call that uses it, exactly as if the call spelled it: a constant default costs no id (g1 = g2), a default holding a class temporary costs its temporaries at each call, the same two ctemps as the spelled-out h(C(1)) (g3 = g4).
cl
il
  *4   0x10   16  ?g0@@YAHH@Z                                  fdef 1, formal 1, label 1, srcfile 1*
  *3   0x16   22  ?g1@@YAHH@Z                                  fdef 1, formal 1, label 1*
  *3   0x16   22  ?g2@@YAHH@Z                                  fdef 1, formal 1, label 1*
  *5   0x2d   45  ?g3@@YAHH@Z                                  ctemp 2, fdef 1, formal 1, label 1*
  *5   0x2d   45  ?g4@@YAHH@Z                                  ctemp 2, fdef 1, formal 1, label 1*
  *3   0x10   16  ?g5@@YAHH@Z                                  fdef 1, formal 1, label 1*
